79. Fix API cache semantics

Your current translation endpoint serves individual compiled records with:

Cache-Control: ... immutable

which is appropriate only when the URL itself identifies an immutable version.

Use:

/v1/works/PTW.../versions/7
→ immutable

But:

/v1/works/PTW...

means current state.

So use:

ETag
revalidation
short/cacheable TTL

not year-long immutable semantics.
80. Fix ETag

Current list translations computes an ETag from effectively the number of works rather than actual projection state.

Two compilations with same count but changed contents can collide semantically.

Use:

projection_content_hash

or:

state_cursor

