90. What this ultimately buys you

Once you build this exact OpenPāṭala, the higher architecture stops being speculative.

The graph automatically produces:

missing translation
→ Factory work

translation disagreement
→ Eval work

identity conflict
→ resolver work

hard unresolved decision
→ scholar work

missing manuscript observation
→ RealityRequest

learner confusion
→ review signal

model failure cluster
→ evolution SystemIssue

That is the bridge from OpenPāṭala 0.5 into the agentic epistemic system we discussed.

The public product is simple:

    Find any Sanskrit work and discover what it is, where it survives, what texts and translations exist, what Pāṭala can legally expose or compute on, and exactly where every piece of information came from.

Internally, however, you're building something more valuable:

    a self-expanding inventory of reality where every missing field becomes machine-addressable work.

That is the version I would now call canonical.